Find $y$, then find $x$. All lengths are in centimetres. Give exact answers.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\coordinate (R) at (2.4,0);\coordinate (Q) at (2.4,1.8);\coordinate (P) at (-1.8,2.4);
\draw (O)--(R) node[midway,below]{$8$}--(Q) node[midway,right]{$6$}--(P) node[midway,above]{$x$}--(O) node[midway,left]{$10$};
\draw (O)--(Q) node[midway,below right]{$y$};
\draw (2.15,0)--(2.15,0.25)--(2.4,0.25);
\draw (-0.15,0.2)--(0.05,0.35)--(0.2,0.15);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find $x$, then find $y$. All lengths are in centimetres. Give exact answers.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.4);\coordinate (B) at (0,0);\coordinate (C) at (1.8,0);\coordinate (D) at (4.2,1.8);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,left]{$8$}--(C) node[midway,below]{$6$}--(D) node[midway,below right]{$y$}--(A) node[midway,above]{$15$};
\draw (A)--(C) node[midway,above right]{$x$};
\draw (0,0.25)--(0.25,0.25)--(0.25,0);
\draw (1.65,0.2)--(1.85,0.35)--(2,0.15);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The trapezium has equal sloping sides. Find $x$ and $y$, then find its perimeter to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(4.5,0) node[midway,below]{$18\text{ cm}$}--(3.5,1.75) node[midway,right]{$y$}--(1,1.75) node[midway,above]{$10\text{ cm}$}--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (1,1.75)--(1,0) node[midway,right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt]{$7\text{ cm}$};\draw[dashed] (3.5,1.75)--(3.5,0);
\path (4,0) node[above]{$x$};
\draw (1,0.2)--(1.2,0.2)--(1.2,0);\draw (3.5,0.2)--(3.7,0.2)--(3.7,0);
\draw (0.35,0.95)--(0.65,0.8);\draw (3.85,0.8)--(4.15,0.95);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the missing sloping side $s$, then find the perimeter of the trapezium to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(4.8,0) node[midway,below]{$24\text{ cm}$}--(3.8,2.4) node[midway,right]{$s$}--(0,2.4) node[midway,above]{$19\text{ cm}$}--cycle;
\path (0,1.2) node[left]{$12\text{ cm}$};\draw[dashed] (3.8,2.4)--(3.8,0);
\draw (0,0.2)--(0.2,0.2)--(0.2,0);\draw (0,2.2)--(0.2,2.2)--(0.2,2.4);\draw (3.8,0.2)--(4,0.2)--(4,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The horizontal diagonal bisects the vertical diagonal at right angles. The marked sides are equal in pairs. Find the two different side lengths, then find the perimeter to $1$ decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-2.4,0)--(0,1.4)--(1.8,0)--(0,-1.4)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (-2.4,0)--(0,0) node[midway,below]{$12\text{ cm}$}--(1.8,0) node[midway,below]{$9\text{ cm}$};\draw[dashed] (0,1.4)--(0,0) node[midway,left]{$7\text{ cm}$}--(0,-1.4);
\draw (0,0.2)--(0.2,0.2)--(0.2,0);
\draw (-1.3,0.87)--(-1.1,0.53);\draw (-1.3,-0.53)--(-1.1,-0.87);
\draw (0.75,0.53)--(0.95,0.87);\draw (0.9,0.43)--(1.1,0.77);\draw (0.75,-0.53)--(0.95,-0.87);\draw (0.9,-0.43)--(1.1,-0.77);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A pipe has radius $17\text{ cm}$. Its water surface is $30\text{ cm}$ wide and lies below the centre. Find the water depth $d$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) circle (2.04);\fill (0,0) circle (1.2pt);
\draw (0,0)--(-1.8,-0.96) node[midway,above left]{$17\text{ cm}$};\draw (-1.8,-0.96)--(1.8,-0.96);
\path (0,-0.96) node[below]{$30\text{ cm}$};\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(0,-0.96);
\draw (0,-0.76)--(0.2,-0.76)--(0.2,-0.96);
\draw[<->] (2.3,-0.96)--(2.3,-2.04) node[midway,right]{$d$};\draw[dashed] (1.8,-0.96)--(2.3,-0.96);\draw[dashed] (0,-2.04)--(2.3,-2.04);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A tower provides signal within a radius of $25\text{ km}$. A straight road is $9\text{ km}$ from the tower. Find the total length $x$ of road within signal range, to $2$ decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) circle (2.5);\fill (0,0) circle (1.2pt);\path (0,0) node[above left]{Tower};
\draw (-2.7,-0.9)--(2.7,-0.9);\path (2.7,-0.9) node[right]{Road};
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(0,-0.9) node[midway,left]{$9\text{ km}$};\draw (0,0)--(2.33238,-0.9) node[midway,above right]{$25\text{ km}$};
\draw (0,-0.7)--(0.2,-0.7)--(0.2,-0.9);
\draw[<->] (-2.33238,-1.25)--(2.33238,-1.25) node[midway,below]{$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
